message: "If you use this software (QinAvalanche Guard) in your research or publication, please cite it using the metadata from this file. Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2."
title: "QinAvalanche Guard — Deterministic Critical-Event Verifiable Computation Laboratory"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-09"
open-source-date: "2026-09-02"

authors:
  - name: "Qin Chen"
    email: ""  # fill in with public contact email if available

keywords:
  - "QinAvalanche"
  - "BTW sandpile"
  - "Bak-Tang-Wiesenfeld"
  - "self-organized criticality"
  - "deterministic computation"
  - "counterfactual risk mapping"
  - "Sha-256 evidence chain"
  - "reproducible simulation"
  - "educational visualization"
  - "GPLv2"
  - "open source"

license:
  - "GPL-2.0-or-later"
  - "GNU General Public License v2.0 (or later); OSI/FSF approved"

license-url: "LICENSE"
disclaimer-url: "DISCLAIMER.md"
dco-url: "CLA.md"

repository-code: "https://github.com/your-github-org-or-user/QinAvalanche"
repository-artifact: "https://github.com/your-github-org-or-user/QinAvalanche/releases"

abstract: |
  QinAvalanche Guard is an open-source (GPL-2.0-or-later), offline-runnable
  HTML5 interactive laboratory implementing the Bak–Tang–Wiesenfeld (BTW)
  sandpile cellular-automaton model with strict integer semantics, SHA-256
  bound state and event hashes, user-visible counterfactual risk heat-maps
  over every possible drop location, and an AI-visual Baseline clearly
  marked as pending blind validation. The software is expressly NOT certified,
  audited, or validated for any safety-critical, regulated, or real-world
  predictive use. See DISCLAIMER.md for full limitations and the file
  LICENSE for the full GNU GPL v2 legal text.

references:
  - type: article
    title: "Self-organized criticality: An explanation of the 1/f noise"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Bak"
        given-names: "Per"
      - family-names: "Tang"
        given-names: "Chao"
      - family-names: "Wiesenfeld"
        given-names: "Kurt"
    journal: "Physical Review Letters"
    volume: 59
    issue: 4
    pages: "381–384"
    date-published: "1987-07-27"
    doi: "10.1103/PhysRevLett.59.381"
